    apply: "Pick one discipline, such as daily Bible reading, and before you do it each day pray, 'Spirit, work in me as I work.' Notice any tendency to pride or guilt, and bring it to Christ. Read Galatians 5:1 and Colossians 2 and thank God for freedom.",
    activity: "Draw two ditches beside a road on the board, labelled 'Laziness' and 'Legalism', with the road labelled 'Grace-empowered effort'. Ask learners to say how each ditch looks in practice and what keeps us on the road. Read Philippians 2:12-13 and discuss.",
    takeHome: "Read Philippians 2:1-18, Colossians 2:6-23, Galatians 5:1-15 and 1 Corinthians 15:9-11. Write about how grace and effort fit together in your life. Memorise Philippians 2:12-13.",
    prayer: "Thank God for his grace and for working in us. Ask for freedom from both laziness and legalism. Pray for dependence on the Spirit.",
